          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Helianthella, the little sunflower, is a genus of North American plants in the family Asteraceae."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": " Species\n Helianthella californica A.Gray - California, Nevada, Oregon\n Helianthella castanea Greene - San Francisco Bay region\n Helianthella ciliata S.F.Blake - Chihuahua\n Helianthella durangensis B.L.Turner - Durango\n Helianthella gypsophila B.L.Turner - Nuevo León, Coahuila\n Helianthella mexicana A.Gray - San Luis Potosí, Zacatecas, etc.\n Helianthella microcephala (A.Gray) A.Gray - Arizona, New Mexico, Colorado, Utah\n Helianthella parryi A.Gray - Arizona, New Mexico, Colorado, Utah\n Helianthella quinquenervis (Hook.) A.Gray - from Coahuila to Oregon + Montana\n Helianthella uniflora (Nutt.) Torr. & A.Gray - from New Mexico to British Columbia"
          }
        ]
      },
